    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14815" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αργος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, name of several Greek cities, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄ. Ἀχαιϊκόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.141
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄ. Πελασγικόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.681
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄργος</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδίον</span>
			 acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.6.9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Dionys.
			</span></i> Epic. ap. <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δ ώτιον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				45
			</span></i>:—hence Adjs. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργεῖος,
				Ἀργολίς, Ἀργολικός,</span> qq.v.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργόλας</span></b> , ὁ,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				41
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				298
			</span></i>.</div>
